> @echasnovski Do you think it'd be worth exploring further and coming up with a solution that actually generalizes well? I wouldn't mind taking on the work and walking with you toward such;

I think I'd be OK with the solution if it is concise, universal, and efficient enough. However, I am not sure there is a good way to satisfy all three.

The best idea I have in mind for this is a 'TextChanged'/'TextChangedI' autocommand (or `nvim_buf_attach()` with `on_lines`) that verifies that all buffer lines have proper structure. Possibly even fixing fixable lines like after `d$` by appending extra space. But at the moment I don't think the problem is bad enough to justify adding this (there are at least *two* reasonable ways to go around this).
